WEBVTT

00:00:01.743 --> 00:00:04.204
Futurama is brought to you by

00:00:04.329 --> 00:00:05.747
Arachno Spores.

00:00:05.831 --> 00:00:08.250
The fatal spore with the funny name.

00:00:37.963 --> 00:00:42.050
Cop Department is real.
The people you see are not actors.

00:00:42.134 --> 00:00:44.344
Most of them aren't even people.

00:00:44.636 --> 00:00:45.804
Come on, man.

00:00:45.888 --> 00:00:47.890
I didn't fire off no laser.

00:00:47.973 --> 00:00:50.475
Then why is there a smoking hole
in your ceiling, sir?

00:00:50.559 --> 00:00:51.560
What?

00:00:52.873 --> 00:00:55.709
Crazy upstairs lady
must have been shooting down.

00:00:55.772 --> 00:00:58.859
Sir, you're on the top floor
of this particular domicile.

00:00:58.942 --> 00:01:02.112
You get that...Camera out of my house.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.530
Just relax, ma'am.

00:01:03.614 --> 00:01:05.699
Sir, sir, put down the lamp.

00:01:05.782 --> 00:01:08.493
Okay, okay. I'm cooperating.

00:01:08.577 --> 00:01:10.495
That's it. Now put up your hands.

00:01:10.579 --> 00:01:11.997
Nice and slow.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.498
Oh, yeah.

00:01:13.582 --> 00:01:15.709
And while you're at it, un-blur your face.

00:01:16.418 --> 00:01:17.419
Oh, man.

00:01:18.045 --> 00:01:19.463
Hey, Bender.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:21.423
I thought you said
you were in this episode.

00:01:21.506 --> 00:01:25.969
Nah, this week I'm on Caught On Tape 3
'Cause of what I did in the coffee pot.

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.598
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

00:01:29.681 --> 00:01:31.642
I'm just going through some things.

00:01:32.476 --> 00:01:33.810
Ooh!

00:01:36.104 --> 00:01:37.439
I'm going in.

00:01:38.857 --> 00:01:41.944
Cop Department will return
after these messages.

00:01:42.027 --> 00:01:45.697
Is today's hectic lifestyle
making you tense and impatient?

00:01:45.781 --> 00:01:47.324
Shut up and get to the point!

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:51.370
Then come relive the carefree
days of yore at Past-O-Rama

00:01:51.453 --> 00:01:53.914
Where old New York comes alive.

00:01:53.997 --> 00:01:57.042
It's like stepping back
into the year 2000.

00:01:57.125 --> 00:01:59.461
Time for the mammoth hunt, dudes.

00:02:04.383 --> 00:02:06.969
Let's disco dance, Hammurabi.

00:02:07.052 --> 00:02:08.762
Dyn-o-mite!

00:02:10.639 --> 00:02:12.891
Located on the former site of Brooklyn.

00:02:12.975 --> 00:02:14.977
Sounds like your kind of place, Fry.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.395
- Want to go?
- Nah.

00:02:16.478 --> 00:02:18.480
If I ever want to go back to the year 2000

00:02:18.564 --> 00:02:19.940
I'll just freeze myself again.

00:02:20.023 --> 00:02:22.609
Come on, Fry. I really wanna see it.

00:02:22.693 --> 00:02:25.362
You know how I yearn for a simpler time.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.948
A time of barn dances and buggy rides

00:02:28.031 --> 00:02:31.493
before life was cheapened by heartless,
high-tech machines.

00:02:31.577 --> 00:02:32.995
But, Bender, you are a...

00:02:33.078 --> 00:02:35.330
La, la, la, la, la, la,
la, la, la, la, la, la!

00:02:39.418 --> 00:02:41.795
Cool. It's just like the good old days.

00:02:41.878 --> 00:02:43.380
Give me your wallet or I'll cut you!

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.176
Leela, get a picture of me being "mugged."

00:02:48.302 --> 00:02:50.721
I'll take the camera, too.

00:02:52.222 --> 00:02:54.725
Learning is fun.

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:56.560
Ooh!

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.270
Ancient Wall Street.

00:03:11.074 --> 00:03:14.494
I direct your attention
to this ancient and mysterious tablet...

00:03:14.745 --> 00:03:16.747
which has yet to be deciphered.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:18.165
Do you know what it means?

00:03:18.248 --> 00:03:19.708
Yeah, I asked a cop once.

00:03:19.791 --> 00:03:21.501
It means, "up yours, kid."

00:03:21.585 --> 00:03:24.796
I got to say I'm really enjoying
the day out with you people.

00:03:25.547 --> 00:03:28.133
Hey, hey! A suicide booth.

00:03:28.216 --> 00:03:29.468
So long, suckers.

00:03:29.551 --> 00:03:30.636
Sorry, Bender.

00:03:30.719 --> 00:03:32.095
That's just a phone booth.

00:03:32.262 --> 00:03:33.847
- Oh.
- What were they used for?

00:03:33.931 --> 00:03:35.766
In New York? Bathrooms.

00:03:35.849 --> 00:03:36.892
Oh.

00:03:37.059 --> 00:03:38.310
I'll be out in a sec.

00:03:44.149 --> 00:03:46.610
"Tokens only." How does this work?

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:47.945
I'll show you.

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.989
Oh! It's a turnstile.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:59.414
What's this? Another bathroom?

00:03:59.498 --> 00:04:02.000
No, it's a mobile apartment with no rent.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:05.379
Come on, Fry. Get up.

00:04:05.462 --> 00:04:07.172
Ah...

00:04:12.386 --> 00:04:17.391
Wow. The burial chamber of the
20th century's greatest spiritual leader,

00:04:17.474 --> 00:04:18.475
Al Sharpton.

00:04:18.642 --> 00:04:20.143
Ooh.

00:04:20.561 --> 00:04:22.604
Now, this guy had taste.

00:04:22.688 --> 00:04:25.732
It says he was mummified
in ceremonial vestments.

00:04:25.857 --> 00:04:28.318
We sometimes called it a jogging suit.

00:04:31.238 --> 00:04:34.741
The traffic jams of old New York
were a public forum

00:04:34.825 --> 00:04:37.244
for the free interchange of opinion.

00:04:38.787 --> 00:04:40.122
Move it, crap-for-brains!

00:04:40.205 --> 00:04:42.749
- Bug off!
- Get home, bastard man!

00:04:42.833 --> 00:04:46.169
It all started with
Gerald Ford's famous invention

00:04:46.253 --> 00:04:50.340
the automo-car, which was powered by
a tank of burning fossils.

00:04:50.424 --> 00:04:53.260
Here we see a 20th-century assembly line

00:04:53.343 --> 00:04:57.139
where cars were constructed
by primitive robots.

00:04:57.347 --> 00:05:01.685
Ooh-gah, ooh-gah, ooh-gah!
Ooh-gah, ooh-gah, ooh-gah!

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:04.396
We've come a long way, baby.

00:05:05.606 --> 00:05:08.525
The fruit of the robots' labor was this...

00:05:08.609 --> 00:05:11.612
The stately 1992 Latura.

00:05:11.695 --> 00:05:13.405
Hey, my girlfriend had one of those.

00:05:13.488 --> 00:05:15.365
Actually, it wasn't hers.
It was her dad's.

00:05:15.449 --> 00:05:16.909
Actually, she wasn't my girlfriend.

00:05:16.992 --> 00:05:19.453
She just lived next door
and never closed her curtains.

00:05:19.536 --> 00:05:21.371
Fry, remember when I told you

00:05:21.455 --> 00:05:23.749
about always ending your stories
a sentence earlier?

00:05:23.832 --> 00:05:25.876
Come on, let's sneak in for a closer look.

00:05:28.837 --> 00:05:31.131
Sir, we don't touch the antiques, sir.

00:05:31.214 --> 00:05:34.801
You don't... Oh... Oh!
I'm sorry, you work here.

00:05:34.885 --> 00:05:37.763
I should have realized from that
ridiculous getup you're wearing.

00:05:37.846 --> 00:05:40.474
Hey, this is from Miller's Outpost...

00:05:40.557 --> 00:05:43.101
I mean, yeah, I work here all right.

00:05:43.185 --> 00:05:46.647
Here. Move this rust bucket
out behind St. Koch's Cathedral.

00:05:50.859 --> 00:05:53.570
Did you drive much
in the 20th century, Fry?

00:05:53.654 --> 00:05:55.405
No. No one in New York drove.

00:05:55.489 --> 00:05:56.823
There was too much traffic.

00:05:58.784 --> 00:06:01.578
Nice. Listen to that baby purr.

00:06:01.662 --> 00:06:02.871
There's a baby in there, huh?

00:06:10.545 --> 00:06:12.589
It's just like riding a bicycle...

00:06:31.817 --> 00:06:34.403
I think I got whiplash.

00:06:34.486 --> 00:06:36.905
You can't have whiplash.
You don't have a neck.

00:06:36.989 --> 00:06:39.199
I meant ass whiplash.

00:06:39.283 --> 00:06:42.244
I'm just glad we hit something.
I thought we'd never stop.

00:06:47.082 --> 00:06:48.709
I think I got whiplash.

00:07:05.392 --> 00:07:07.060
How's that robot I ran over?

00:07:07.144 --> 00:07:09.187
We did all we could.

00:07:09.271 --> 00:07:10.439
You mean he's...

00:07:10.522 --> 00:07:12.900
Good as new? Yes.

00:07:12.983 --> 00:07:17.446
Leela, Zoidberg, the rest of you,
this is Flexo.

00:07:17.529 --> 00:07:19.197
Sweet llamas of the Bahamas!

00:07:19.281 --> 00:07:20.949
Except for that stylish beard,

00:07:21.033 --> 00:07:22.409
he look just like Bender.

00:07:22.492 --> 00:07:23.952
No duh, dreadlock,

00:07:24.036 --> 00:07:25.203
we're both bending units.

00:07:25.287 --> 00:07:27.372
Hey, bro-bot, what's your serial number?

00:07:27.456 --> 00:07:29.291
3-3-7-0-3-1-8.

00:07:29.374 --> 00:07:33.211
No way. Mine's 2-7-1-6-0-5-7.

00:07:36.256 --> 00:07:37.299
I don't get it.

00:07:37.382 --> 00:07:40.219
We're both expressible
as the sum of two cubes.

00:07:40.427 --> 00:07:41.553
Whoo!

00:07:41.845 --> 00:07:43.263
So, uh, Flexo,

00:07:43.347 --> 00:07:45.390
sorry about crushing your body like that.

00:07:45.474 --> 00:07:46.475
You okay now?

00:07:46.558 --> 00:07:48.727
Well, I don't feel as bad as you look.

00:07:51.188 --> 00:07:53.065
I'm just messing with you, kid.

00:07:53.148 --> 00:07:54.149
You're all right.

00:07:54.233 --> 00:07:55.734
That's some face you got, though.

00:07:55.817 --> 00:07:57.277
I think they got a cream for that.

00:07:59.112 --> 00:08:00.322
No, you're great.

00:08:00.405 --> 00:08:01.448
Well, just let me know

00:08:01.531 --> 00:08:03.617
if there's anything I can do
to make it up to you.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:06.370
Actually, your little stunt
did a number on my back.

00:08:06.453 --> 00:08:07.788
You mind rubbing it for me?

00:08:07.871 --> 00:08:09.122
Uh... Sure.

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:12.209
Oh, yeah, that's it. Little lower.

00:08:12.292 --> 00:08:13.710
- How's that?
- Lower.

00:08:14.211 --> 00:08:16.505
Yeah, that's getting it.
Little lower, though.

00:08:16.588 --> 00:08:18.257
I can't get any lower than this.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:20.884
I'll say. You're rubbing my ass.

00:08:27.891 --> 00:08:29.601
Hey, check it out here.

00:08:29.685 --> 00:08:31.353
Six beautiful devices.

00:08:31.436 --> 00:08:33.480
They know what you like and they'll do it

00:08:33.564 --> 00:08:36.066
to within a tolerance of one micron.

00:08:37.901 --> 00:08:39.903
- Spin those fans, baby!
- Baby! Whoo!

00:08:40.862 --> 00:08:42.489
All right, mama!

00:08:43.365 --> 00:08:44.575
Spin it, baby.

00:08:51.248 --> 00:08:52.499
I don't like this place.

00:08:52.583 --> 00:08:55.335
It's 120 degrees
and there's very little oxygen.

00:08:55.419 --> 00:08:56.753
Shut up and hoot.

00:09:08.348 --> 00:09:10.684
Hubba-hubba. She is built...

00:09:10.767 --> 00:09:12.561
In Mexico, I believe.

00:09:12.644 --> 00:09:14.354
And that ain't silicon.

00:09:14.438 --> 00:09:16.815
It's tungsten, and plenty of it.

00:09:17.024 --> 00:09:19.568
Yeah. Look at that exhaust fan.

00:09:20.819 --> 00:09:22.029
Pervert.

00:09:22.112 --> 00:09:24.072
Yoo-hoo!

00:09:25.824 --> 00:09:27.951
Oh.

00:09:28.201 --> 00:09:29.870
Thanks, moderate spender.

00:09:29.953 --> 00:09:32.205
Please select erotic transaction.

00:09:32.289 --> 00:09:35.375
Yeah. How about a lap dance
for my pal here?

00:09:35.542 --> 00:09:38.128
Ooh! Yeah. Chuck-a-chong.

00:09:39.046 --> 00:09:40.756
No, no, that's all right, really.

00:09:42.257 --> 00:09:44.384
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:09:47.137 --> 00:09:50.432
I'm telling you. There's something
about Flexo I don't like.

00:09:51.016 --> 00:09:52.643
Hey, Fry, think fast.

00:09:55.145 --> 00:09:56.688
Get it? It's chlorine.

00:10:01.318 --> 00:10:03.737
It's funny because it's poisonous.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:06.573
Yeah, keep laughing, brine shrimp,
but he's bad news.

00:10:06.657 --> 00:10:08.200
I regret ever running him over.

00:10:08.283 --> 00:10:09.826
Take a rage dump, mon.

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:11.370
He's no worse than Bender.

00:10:11.453 --> 00:10:13.538
He's much worse. He drinks and smokes

00:10:13.622 --> 00:10:15.874
and he posts naked pictures of me
on the Internet.

00:10:15.958 --> 00:10:17.167
That's Bender all right.

00:10:17.251 --> 00:10:18.752
I'm talking about Flexo.

00:10:19.002 --> 00:10:21.630
Oh, I get it. This is cute.

00:10:21.713 --> 00:10:23.799
You're jealous of Bender's new friend.

00:10:23.882 --> 00:10:24.883
No, I'm not.

00:10:24.967 --> 00:10:28.011
Mark my words. Flexo's evil.

00:10:28.095 --> 00:10:30.347
He's the evil Bender.

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:31.974
Rage dump.

00:10:33.141 --> 00:10:34.476
Good news, everyone.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:37.980
Report to my bedroom
for a private exhibition.

00:10:38.105 --> 00:10:39.523
Hmm.

00:10:39.606 --> 00:10:41.567
Everyone get in bed with me.

00:10:41.650 --> 00:10:44.278
I have something to show you.

00:10:47.823 --> 00:10:50.909
Feast your eyes on this!

00:10:52.369 --> 00:10:54.204
It's beautiful.

00:10:54.288 --> 00:10:55.539
And huge.

00:10:55.622 --> 00:10:56.957
Can I touch it?

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:58.709
So, what is it already?

00:10:58.792 --> 00:11:01.295
It's a single atom of jumbonium.

00:11:01.378 --> 00:11:02.713
An element so rare,

00:11:02.796 --> 00:11:06.341
The nucleus alone is worth
more than $50,000.

00:11:06.425 --> 00:11:08.427
- How much more?
- $100,000.

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:11.263
That's why I hid it here,
under my mattress.

00:11:11.346 --> 00:11:14.141
Professor, can we discuss this
somewhere else?

00:11:14.224 --> 00:11:15.767
Why, certainly.

00:11:16.393 --> 00:11:19.313
The atom sits atop this dime-store tiara

00:11:19.396 --> 00:11:23.066
which will be awarded to the winner
of this year's Miss Universe pageant

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:25.110
on the planet Tova nine.

00:11:25.569 --> 00:11:28.655
Your job is to deliver it safe and sound.

00:11:28.906 --> 00:11:33.076
Wow! When I was a little girl on Mars
I dreamed of being Miss Universe.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:34.411
That's kind of pathetic.

00:11:34.494 --> 00:11:35.537
Oh, come on, Leela.

00:11:35.621 --> 00:11:37.998
Deep down, all girls
want to be Miss Universe.

00:11:38.081 --> 00:11:39.416
- Not me.
- Really?

00:11:39.499 --> 00:11:41.043
Maybe it's just cute girls.

00:11:42.044 --> 00:11:44.421
Due to the atom's tremendous value,

00:11:44.504 --> 00:11:47.424
