00:12:31.301 --> 00:12:34.638
Okay. First Bender, then Flexo, then Fry.

00:12:34.721 --> 00:12:36.265
Flexo outranks me?

00:12:36.348 --> 00:12:38.850
That's "Flexo outranks me, sir."

00:12:43.772 --> 00:12:45.023
Halt! Who goes there?

00:12:45.107 --> 00:12:46.275
Don't point that at me.

00:12:46.358 --> 00:12:47.359
Fry who?

00:12:47.442 --> 00:12:49.236
Look, I know Flexo's your friend,

00:12:49.319 --> 00:12:51.446
but I don't trust him alone with the atom.

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:52.531
My God, Fry.

00:12:52.614 --> 00:12:55.576
Just 'cause the guy's got
a beard, you label him as evil?

00:12:55.659 --> 00:12:57.536
Well, I got a label for you, pal.

00:12:57.619 --> 00:12:59.955
An ugly little word called "prejudice."

00:13:00.038 --> 00:13:01.248
I'm not prejudiced.

00:13:01.331 --> 00:13:03.834
Save it for the cross burning, Adolf.

00:13:08.547 --> 00:13:09.923
Keeping an eye on the safe?

00:13:10.007 --> 00:13:11.008
You know it.

00:13:12.259 --> 00:13:14.094
Well, looks like it's my shift.

00:13:14.177 --> 00:13:16.597
You lie down and go off-line for a while.

00:13:16.763 --> 00:13:18.515
All right.

00:13:28.317 --> 00:13:29.401
Caught you!

00:13:29.484 --> 00:13:31.278
I saw you looking at the atom.

00:13:31.361 --> 00:13:33.739
So? I look at lots of atoms.

00:13:33.822 --> 00:13:35.949
Shouldn't you be resting up
for your shift?

00:13:36.033 --> 00:13:38.535
Oh, you'd like it if I went to sleep,
wouldn't you?

00:13:38.619 --> 00:13:40.704
Whatever it takes to shut your yapper.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:43.957
No, I'm just kidding. You're a joker.

00:13:44.041 --> 00:13:45.500
Yeah? Well, here's a funny joke.

00:13:45.584 --> 00:13:47.753
I'm going to sit right here
till it's my shift.

00:13:47.836 --> 00:13:49.379
Suit yourself, skinbag.

00:13:49.463 --> 00:13:50.464
That I will.

00:13:50.547 --> 00:13:51.673
- Good.
- Good.

00:13:51.757 --> 00:13:52.883
- Good.
- Good.

00:13:52.966 --> 00:13:54.092
- Good.
- Good.

00:13:55.177 --> 00:13:56.428
Good.

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:01.934
Well, that's eight hours.

00:14:02.017 --> 00:14:04.311
Yeah, eight hours of solid boredom.

00:14:04.394 --> 00:14:05.854
Nah, I'm kidding.

00:14:05.938 --> 00:14:07.439
You're a wonderful man.

00:14:09.483 --> 00:14:11.610
Finally, the atom is safe.

00:14:26.625 --> 00:14:28.794
Huh?

00:14:31.922 --> 00:14:35.008
What is it? My God!

00:14:35.092 --> 00:14:36.718
- Did you hear maracas?
- No.

00:14:36.802 --> 00:14:38.470
Then it wasn't space banditos.

00:14:38.554 --> 00:14:39.972
Bender, lock down the ship.

00:14:40.055 --> 00:14:41.348
Don't let Flexo escape.

00:14:41.431 --> 00:14:42.724
Aye, aye, captain.

00:14:42.808 --> 00:14:45.769
It appears that Flexo
has outwitted us all.

00:14:46.019 --> 00:14:49.231
Especially me... Bender.

00:14:54.194 --> 00:14:56.196
How could Flexo have stolen the atom?

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:57.906
He must have used a sleep ray on me.

00:14:57.990 --> 00:14:59.700
Sleep rays exist in the future, right?

00:14:59.783 --> 00:15:00.784
No.

00:15:00.867 --> 00:15:02.202
Then I must have fallen asleep.

00:15:02.286 --> 00:15:04.705
Well, you were sure right
about Flexo being evil.

00:15:04.788 --> 00:15:07.874
I locked down the exits,
but he may have already gotten away.

00:15:07.958 --> 00:15:10.961
Okay, thanks, Bender.
Let's fan out and look for him.

00:15:11.044 --> 00:15:13.672
Roger that.
I got a map of the ship right here.

00:15:14.089 --> 00:15:15.465
Keep an eye on Fry.

00:15:15.549 --> 00:15:18.218
We can't rule out the possibility
that he did it.

00:15:23.891 --> 00:15:25.267
Aha!

00:15:27.853 --> 00:15:29.479
Aha!

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:31.064
Searching.

00:15:31.231 --> 00:15:32.274
Hmm.

00:15:32.357 --> 00:15:34.818
Fry, why are you looking for Flexo

00:15:34.902 --> 00:15:36.486
in my underpants drawer?

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:38.280
I didn't find him here ten minutes ago

00:15:38.363 --> 00:15:40.198
so I thought it was time to check again.

00:15:40.282 --> 00:15:41.950
Ow!

00:15:42.117 --> 00:15:44.786
Well, he wasn't in the, uh, kitchen room.

00:15:45.704 --> 00:15:48.540
Say, Bender, can I hold that map
for a second?

00:15:48.624 --> 00:15:51.752
And leave me high and dry
in case of a scavenger hunt?

00:15:51.835 --> 00:15:53.170
I think not.

00:15:53.253 --> 00:15:54.254
Give it up!

00:15:57.507 --> 00:15:59.343
All right! Take it. Sheesh!

00:16:04.723 --> 00:16:07.351
Well, looks like Flexo got away clean.

00:16:07.434 --> 00:16:08.894
It's a darn shame.

00:16:08.977 --> 00:16:12.189
He must have jumped ship
with the atom the second we landed.

00:16:12.272 --> 00:16:15.442
Or maybe... he never left at all!

00:16:16.443 --> 00:16:18.195
Wait a minute. You're Bender.

00:16:18.278 --> 00:16:19.988
Of course. Who said I wasn't?

00:16:20.072 --> 00:16:22.824
But why were you wearing that scarf,
and the turtleneck,

00:16:22.908 --> 00:16:24.243
and this fruity number?

00:16:24.326 --> 00:16:26.453
It's a little thing called style.

00:16:26.536 --> 00:16:28.163
Look it up sometime.

00:16:42.052 --> 00:16:45.722
Our ninth finalist, Miss Methane planet,

00:16:46.056 --> 00:16:48.308
Halatina Smogmeyer.

00:16:53.981 --> 00:16:56.650
And our tenth and final finalist,

00:16:56.733 --> 00:17:00.487
Miss Earth's Moon, The Crushinator.

00:17:03.156 --> 00:17:05.075
Thank you, Bob Barker.

00:17:05.158 --> 00:17:08.996
I'm as happy as a girl can be.
End statement.

00:17:09.079 --> 00:17:11.123
Which one of these lovely womanoids

00:17:11.206 --> 00:17:13.625
will take home the atomic tiara?

00:17:14.793 --> 00:17:16.545
Downplay the tiara.

00:17:16.628 --> 00:17:18.422
Uh... We'll find out

00:17:18.505 --> 00:17:21.091
after these subliminal messages.

00:17:23.844 --> 00:17:25.846
So you lost the atom, huh?

00:17:25.929 --> 00:17:28.348
You're garbage, human garbage!

00:17:28.432 --> 00:17:31.059
Do you brain-dead space jockeys
have any idea

00:17:31.143 --> 00:17:32.686
how much that thing is worth?

00:17:32.769 --> 00:17:34.730
- $100,000?
- $200,000?

00:17:34.813 --> 00:17:36.315
$200,001?

00:17:36.398 --> 00:17:38.358
You're closest without going over.

00:17:38.442 --> 00:17:39.818
Well, we'll be leaving now.

00:17:39.902 --> 00:17:42.529
If you could just sign this form saying
you received the atom.

00:17:42.613 --> 00:17:43.906
I'm not signing squat.

00:17:43.989 --> 00:17:46.783
You find me that damn tiara
before the pageant ends.

00:17:46.867 --> 00:17:48.994
- But, Mr. Barker...
- Enough out of you!

00:17:49.077 --> 00:17:50.871
I may be against the fur industry.

00:17:50.954 --> 00:17:53.707
But that won't stop me
from skinning you alive.

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:55.459
As long as no one wears the skin.

00:17:57.961 --> 00:18:00.672
Well, gentlemen, it appears we're boned.

00:18:02.382 --> 00:18:03.800
- Hey!
- Flexo!

00:18:03.884 --> 00:18:04.885
Get him!

00:18:16.772 --> 00:18:21.068
Next up, in what is generously
called "the talent competition"

00:18:21.151 --> 00:18:25.572
performing a traditional gangster rap,
Miss... what the...

00:18:28.367 --> 00:18:29.368
Got ya!

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:34.581
Fight! Fight! Fight! Fight! Fight!

00:18:34.665 --> 00:18:36.875
Shoot him! He's choking me!

00:18:36.959 --> 00:18:39.544
No, shoot him! He's choking me!

00:18:41.672 --> 00:18:43.548
I don't know which one to shoot.

00:18:43.632 --> 00:18:45.342
Flexo! Shoot Flexo.

00:18:53.308 --> 00:18:55.102
Women only room!

00:19:05.028 --> 00:19:06.780
All right, enough of this.

00:19:18.417 --> 00:19:19.751
There's the atom!

00:19:21.086 --> 00:19:22.504
Aw, geez.

00:19:22.588 --> 00:19:24.715
Bender? You stole the atom?

00:19:24.798 --> 00:19:27.885
Yeah, but I can explain.
It's very valuable.

00:19:27.968 --> 00:19:30.721
I saw him snatch it while Fry was asleep.

00:19:30.804 --> 00:19:33.265
That's why I ran to tell Bob Barker.

00:19:33.348 --> 00:19:34.933
Whoa, whoa! Wait a second.

00:19:35.017 --> 00:19:36.935
You mean Bender is the evil Bender?

00:19:37.019 --> 00:19:39.021
I am shocked, shocked!

00:19:39.104 --> 00:19:40.480
Well, not that shocked.

00:19:40.564 --> 00:19:42.900
I'm sorry we suspected you, Flexo.

00:19:42.983 --> 00:19:45.110
It's just, what with the beard and all...

00:19:45.193 --> 00:19:47.821
Don't even bother. You people sicken me.

00:19:47.905 --> 00:19:50.198
I put my life on the line
to guard that atom

00:19:50.282 --> 00:19:51.742
and this is how you repay me?

00:19:51.825 --> 00:19:54.870
Well, you can go rot for all I care.

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:58.832
Nah, I'm just kidding.
You guys are all right.

00:20:01.668 --> 00:20:03.128
I'm so confused.

00:20:03.211 --> 00:20:05.297
The Bender I liked turned out to be evil,

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:07.382
and the Bender I hated was good.

00:20:07.841 --> 00:20:11.386
How can I live my life
when I can't tell good from evil?

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:14.473
They're both fine choices.
Whatever floats your boat.

00:20:17.434 --> 00:20:18.560
Is this the guy?

00:20:18.644 --> 00:20:19.728
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:20:19.811 --> 00:20:21.146
That looks like him, whatever.

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:23.273
- Wait! But...
- Take him away.

00:20:25.901 --> 00:20:28.779
Okay, let's put an end
to this pathetic hoedown.

00:20:28.862 --> 00:20:30.280
Brannigan, read the thing.

00:20:30.364 --> 00:20:31.865
And the winner is...

00:20:32.699 --> 00:20:33.951
It figures.

00:20:34.034 --> 00:20:36.203
Who else but Zapp Brannigan
would be judging

00:20:36.286 --> 00:20:39.289
the most chauvinistic,
degrading, dehumanizing...

00:20:39.373 --> 00:20:40.374
"Leela"?

00:20:42.709 --> 00:20:44.211
Wait, you're making a...

00:20:44.586 --> 00:20:45.796
Ooh.

00:20:45.879 --> 00:20:47.214
Look at that.

00:20:48.924 --> 00:20:50.717
I feel like a princess!

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:59.142
Wait, what are you people, idiots?

00:20:59.226 --> 00:21:01.728
I'm still going mano a mano
with this envelope.

00:21:06.233 --> 00:21:07.859
And the winner is...

00:21:07.943 --> 00:21:09.903
Miss Vega 4.

00:21:19.204 --> 00:21:21.456
There it is

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:25.335
Miss Universe

00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:28.880
There it is

00:21:28.964 --> 00:21:32.718
Looking weird

00:21:33.719 --> 00:21:35.971
I almost had that tiara.

00:21:36.221 --> 00:21:37.723
Me, too.

00:21:37.806 --> 00:21:40.642
Well, you guys might both be losers,
but I just made out

00:21:40.726 --> 00:21:43.270
With that radiator woman
from the radiator planet.

00:21:43.562 --> 00:21:45.647
Fry, that's a radiator.

00:21:45.939 --> 00:21:48.108
Oh.

00:21:48.191 --> 00:21:50.485
Is there a burn ward
within ten feet of here?